From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: asus-rog5-ams678: keep a brightness set while the panel is off

update_status returned -EPERM before the panel was prepared. Once the kernel
fbdev client was dropped (its modeset at msm probe lit the panel early), the
boot-time systemd-backlight restore always hit that, failed and retried to
its start limit, and the panel came up at brightness 0. Report success
instead: the backlight core already stored the level, and drm_panel_enable()
applies it through backlight_enable() once the panel is on.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c	2026-09-26 18:19:02.736903014 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-asus-rog5-ams678.c	2026-09-26 18:19:02.749424985 +0200
@@ -398,8 +398,15 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&ctx->lock);
 	if (!ctx->initialized) {
+		/*
+		 * Panel off: keep the requested level (the core stored it in
+		 * props) and report success. drm_panel_enable() applies it via
+		 * backlight_enable() once the panel is on, so a brightness
+		 * restore before the first modeset (systemd-backlight at boot)
+		 * is not lost and does not fail.
+		 */
 		mutex_unlock(&ctx->lock);
-		return -EPERM;
+		return 0;
 	}
 	mode_flags = dsi->mode_flags;
 	/*
